# Hand-written placeholder -- boston+ivy.obj's own "mtllib boston ivy.mtl"
# reference has a space in the filename, which this project's fscanf("%s",
# ...) token parser can't read past (it would only ever capture "boston",
# not "ivy.mtl"). Renamed the mtllib line inside the .obj to
# "boston_ivy.mtl" (no space) and wrote this file to match. No texture/mtl
# was actually bundled with the download either, so both materials are
# plain solid colors instead: wire_228184153 is the backing box the ivy
# grows on, wire_141007058 is the ivy leaves themselves.

newmtl wire_228184153
Ka 0.150000 0.140000 0.120000
Kd 0.420000 0.380000 0.320000
Ks 0.050000 0.050000 0.050000
Ke 0.000000 0.000000 0.000000
Ns 8.000000
d 1.000000

newmtl wire_141007058
Ka 0.080000 0.150000 0.060000
Kd 0.220000 0.420000 0.150000
Ks 0.050000 0.050000 0.050000
Ke 0.000000 0.000000 0.000000
Ns 8.000000
d 1.000000
